ut ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUCursed be he that lieth with any manner of beast. And all the people shall say, Amen.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡Cursed be he that lieth with his sister, the daughter of his father, or the daughter of his mother. And all the people shall say, Amen.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSCursed be he that lieth with his mother in law. And all the people shall say, Amen.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUCursed be he that smiteth his neighbour secretly. And all the people shall say, Amen.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_Cursed be he that taketh reward to slay an innocent person. And all the people shall say, Amen.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjCursed be he that confirmeth not all the words of this law to do them. And all the people shall say, Amen.¦layout ªlast_verse